{"version":"1","id":"golangexample","handle":"golangexample","name":"Golang Example","image":"https://media.daily.dev/image/upload/t_logo,f_auto/v1/logos/a2ba12f3f1184e329cff6fc41dbb80ab","description":null,"is_squad":false,"x":-0.996,"y":-5.3155,"cluster_id":3,"posts_collected":418,"newest_post_at":"2022-01-02T08:02:00.000Z","oldest_post_at":"2021-09-08T04:22:38.000Z","features":{"hype_score":0.0,"listicle_ratio":0.0,"question_ratio":0.0,"avg_read_time":3.057416,"summary_length_avg":293.551378,"title_length_avg":60.356459,"title_length_var":529.157626,"tag_entropy":4.125847,"tag_diversity":0.38756,"top_tag_share":0.191388,"avg_upvotes":0.090909,"median_upvotes":0.0,"avg_comments":0.0,"comment_to_upvote_ratio":0.025641,"zero_engagement_share":0.937799,"viral_share":0.0,"posts_per_week":25.188557,"non_article_ratio":0.0,"author_present_share":0.0,"recency_skew":28.857143},"view_coords":{"engagement_style":[-8.1912,-7.3088],"cadence_depth":[7.9559,-6.4559],"hype_variety":[-7.8529,7.9412],"title_style":[-7.8529,-1.7941]},"top_tags":[["golang",130],["general-programming",72],["kubernetes",20],["testing",20],["cloud",18],["backend",18],["docker",17],["logging",14]],"sample_titles":{"representative":["An HTTP toolkit for security research","A vulnerability scanner for container images and filesystems","GoLang Web Assembly bindings for DOM, HTML etc"],"outlier":["Scanner to send specially crafted requests and catch callbacks of systems that are impacted by Log4J Log4Shell vulnerability (CVE-2021-44228)"]},"recent_posts":[{"id":"wE6l_fWem","title":"Tcpmeter - a tool for measuring TCP upload and download speeds and RTT latency","url":"https://golangexample.com/tcpmeter-a-tool-for-measuring-tcp-upload-and-download-speeds-and-rtt-latency/","comments_permalink":"https://app.daily.dev/posts/tcpmeter---a-tool-for-measuring-tcp-upload-and-download-speeds-and-rtt-latency-we6l-fwem","summary":"tcpmeter is a tool for measuring TCP upload and download speeds and RTT latency. It can be used to test the speed of a web server and a web browser. It is available on GitHub under the MIT license. For more information, visit: http://www.tcpmeter.com.","image":"https://media.daily.dev/image/upload/f_auto,q_auto/v1/posts/cc1b2cae81bf4f70e5743de1bfcec175","num_upvotes":0,"num_comments":0,"created_at":"2022-01-02T08:02:00.000Z"},{"id":"2GJDts2qN","title":"Region quadtrees and efficient neighbour finding techniques in Go","url":"https://golangexample.com/region-quadtrees-and-efficient-neighbour-finding-techniques-in-go/","comments_permalink":"https://app.daily.dev/posts/region-quadtrees-and-efficient-neighbour-finding-techniques-in-go-2gjdts2qn","summary":"Region quadtrees are a special kind of quadtree that recursively subdivides a 2 dimensional space into 4 smaller and generally equal rectangular regions. A leaf node represents a rectangular region of an image in which all colors are equal or the color difference is under a given threshold. A quadtree can also be used to represent data fields with variable resolution.","image":"https://media.daily.dev/image/upload/f_auto,q_auto/v1/posts/eb61c246abe5a5bfaa96b005adf95c1e","num_upvotes":0,"num_comments":0,"created_at":"2022-01-02T08:01:00.000Z"},{"id":"rdY3a6V8T","title":"Unlock Music Project - CLI Edition","url":"https://golangexample.com/unlock-music-project-cli-edition/","comments_permalink":"https://app.daily.dev/posts/unlock-music-project---cli-edition-rdy3a6v8t","summary":"Unlock Music Project \u2013 CLI Edition. Unlock Music Project is a free and open-source software project. The project uses Golang 1.16. It is intended to be used on computers with a 64-bit version of the operating system. For more information, visit the project's GitHub page.","image":"https://media.daily.dev/image/upload/f_auto,q_auto/v1/posts/eb61c246abe5a5bfaa96b005adf95c1e","num_upvotes":1,"num_comments":0,"created_at":"2022-01-02T08:00:00.000Z"},{"id":"DcOgvUAfv","title":"A native Go clean room implementation of the Porter Stemming algorithm","url":"https://golangexample.com/a-native-go-clean-room-implementation-of-the-porter-stemming-algorithm/","comments_permalink":"https://app.daily.dev/posts/a-native-go-clean-room-implementation-of-the-porter-stemming-algorithm-dcogvuafv","summary":"A native Go clean room implementation of the Porter Stemming Algorithm. This algorithm is of interest to people doing Machine Learning or Natural Language Processing (NLP) This is NOT a port. This is a native Go implementation from the human-readable description of the algorithm. I\u2019ve tried to make it (more) efficient by NOT internally using string\u2019s, but instead internally using []rune.","image":"https://media.daily.dev/image/upload/f_auto,q_auto/v1/posts/eb61c246abe5a5bfaa96b005adf95c1e","num_upvotes":0,"num_comments":0,"created_at":"2022-01-02T08:00:00.000Z"},{"id":"n0CQqlxyo","title":"An open-source project for 5th generation (5G) mobile core networks","url":"https://golangexample.com/an-open-source-project-for-5th-generation-5g-mobile-core-networks/","comments_permalink":"https://app.daily.dev/posts/an-open-source-project-for-5th-generation-5g-mobile-core-networks-n0cqqlxyo","summary":"Free5GC is an open-source project for 5th generation (5G) mobile core networks. The ultimate goal of this project is to implement the 5G core network (5GC) defined in 3GPP Release 15 (R15) and beyond.Detailed changes for each release are documented in the release notes.","image":"https://media.daily.dev/image/upload/f_auto,q_auto/v1/posts/eb61c246abe5a5bfaa96b005adf95c1e","num_upvotes":1,"num_comments":0,"created_at":"2022-01-02T08:00:00.000Z"},{"id":"k2LdfPBTK","title":"MailHog SMTP Protocol For Golang","url":"https://golangexample.com/mailhog-smtp-protocol-for-golang/","comments_permalink":"https://app.daily.dev/posts/mailhog-smtp-protocol-for-golang-k2ldfpbtk","summary":"MailHog SMTP Protocol implements an SMTP server state machine. It attempts to encapsulate as much of the SMTP protocol (plus its extensions) as possible without compromising configurability or requiring specific backend implementations. The state machine provides hooks to manipulate its behaviour.","image":"https://media.daily.dev/image/upload/f_auto,q_auto/v1/posts/eb61c246abe5a5bfaa96b005adf95c1e","num_upvotes":0,"num_comments":0,"created_at":"2022-01-02T07:53:00.000Z"},{"id":"YS0rPJ9w9","title":"An Encrypted overlay filesystem written in Golang","url":"https://golangexample.com/an-encrypted-overlay-filesystem-written-in-golang/","comments_permalink":"https://app.daily.dev/posts/an-encrypted-overlay-filesystem-written-in-golang-ys0rpj9w9","summary":"Gocryptfs is an encrypted overlay filesystem written in Go. It was inspired by EncFS and strives to fix its security issues while providing good performance (benchmarks) It has gone through hours and hours of stress (fsstress, extractloop.bash) and correctness testing. It is now considered ready for general consumption.","image":"https://media.daily.dev/image/upload/f_auto,q_auto/v1/posts/c3dd2aac72a69cdca56abbc00dcea05e","num_upvotes":0,"num_comments":0,"created_at":"2022-01-02T07:52:00.000Z"},{"id":"Ykt56sdbG","title":"Go library for writing standalone Map/Reduce jobs or for use with Hadoop's streaming protocol","url":"https://golangexample.com/go-library-for-writing-standalone-map-reduce-jobs-or-for-use-with-hadoops-streaming-protocol/","comments_permalink":"https://app.daily.dev/posts/go-library-for-writing-standalone-map-reduce-jobs-or-for-use-with-hadoop-s-streaming-protocol-ykt56sdbg","summary":"dmrgo is a Go library for writing map/reduce jobs. It can be used with Hadoop's streaming protocol, but also includes a standalone map/ reduce implementation. It is partially based on ideas from Yelp's MrJob package for Python. The traditional \"word count\" example is in the examples directory.","image":"https://media.daily.dev/image/upload/f_auto,q_auto/v1/posts/eb61c246abe5a5bfaa96b005adf95c1e","num_upvotes":1,"num_comments":0,"created_at":"2022-01-02T07:52:00.000Z"},{"id":"OJjWTbCqf","title":"Ghw - a small Golang library providing hardware inspection and discovery for Linux and Windows","url":"https://golangexample.com/ghw-a-small-golang-library-providing-hardware-inspection-and-discovery-for-linux-and-windows/","comments_permalink":"https://app.daily.dev/posts/ghw---a-small-golang-library-providing-hardware-inspection-and-discovery-for-linux-and-windows-ojjwtbcqf","summary":"ghw is a small Golang library providing hardware inspection and discovery for Linux and Windows. There currently exists partial support for MacOSX. ghw does NOT report information that is temporary or variable. It is NOT a system monitor nor is it an appropriate tool for gathering data points for metrics.","image":"https://media.daily.dev/image/upload/f_auto,q_auto/v1/posts/eb61c246abe5a5bfaa96b005adf95c1e","num_upvotes":0,"num_comments":0,"created_at":"2022-01-02T07:51:00.000Z"},{"id":"-ZoORPsDB","title":"Gocontracts - A tool for design-by-contract in Golang","url":"https://golangexample.com/gocontracts-a-tool-for-design-by-contract-in-golang/","comments_permalink":"https://app.daily.dev/posts/gocontracts---a-tool-for-design-by-contract-in-golang--zoorpsdb","summary":"gocontracts is a tool for design-by-contract in Go. It generates pre- and post-condition checks from the function descriptions so that the contracts are included in the documentation and automatically reflected in the code. Each contract is defined as a one-line item in a bulleted list. It does not validate the correctness of the conditions.","image":"https://media.daily.dev/image/upload/f_auto,q_auto/v1/posts/eb61c246abe5a5bfaa96b005adf95c1e","num_upvotes":0,"num_comments":0,"created_at":"2022-01-02T07:50:00.000Z"}],"similar_handles":["clper","alternativeto","rubyflow","dr","slidebean"],"opposite_handles":["dailydevworld","horde","on_leuwcq","watercooler","dotnetsquad"],"similar":[{"id":"clper","handle":"clper","name":"Cloud Perspectives","is_squad":false,"x":-1.0744,"y":-5.104